  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120882,
      "SummaryText": "The following is a summary of the six elements of the Risk Management Program as part of our 5-year update that has been implemented at the Harcros facility located at 4330 Geraldine Avenue, St. Louis, MO 63115. The changes in this RMP update include the recently updated PHA, which has formatting changes and a more detailed human factors review. The RMP also includes several updated dates and updated executive summary.\n\n1. Accidental release prevention and emergency response policies\nOur emergency response program is a detailed response plan for any releases/exposures to aqueous ammonia. The site does have HAZWOPER trained employees. The emergency response plan includes procedures for notification of the local fire authority and notification of our immediate neighbors.\n\n2. Stationary source and regulated substances handled\nThe facility handles one chemical above the RMP threshold limits: Ammonia (20% or greater). The aqueous ammonia is stored in 55 gallon drums and 330 gal totes. The chemical is neither packaged or used at this facility.\n\n3. Accidental release prevention program\nDue to the storage and handling of aqueous ammonia, this site falls under RMP Program Level 2. An original Process Hazard Analysis was conducted and those corrective actions have been closed. The facility revalidated the Process Hazard Analysis in 2025 and all corrective actions were completed in February, 2025. The accidental release prevention program includes, but is not limited to, access control and security of the site; checking prepackaged containers that cross their docks for tampering and damage, as per the standard operating procedure, and emergency response.\n\n4. 5-Year accident history\nNo RMP process-related accidents have occurred at this facility within the last five years.\n\n5. Emergency Response program\nThe facility's emergency response is outlined in their specific Emergency Action and Emergency Response Plans which includes responding to aqueous ammonia releases, onsite only."
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000120882,
      "SummaryText": "The Harcros team members that would respond to releases of RMP chemicals are HAZWOPER trained. Harcros works closely with our suppliers, customers, and public responders to continuously improve our emergency response capabilities.\n\n6. Planned changes to improve safety\nHarcros continues to participate in the National Association of Chemical Distributor's programs, and although no specific safety improvements are scheduled at this time, we continue to improve our operations in accordance\nwith Responsible Distribution Guidelines. Frequent site inspections and audits are completed in order to identify any safety improvements needed."
    }
  ]
